From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mindone <mindone@localhost>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] telephony: power off the radio of a phone without a
 subscription

When config_powerOffRadioWhenNoActiveSubscription is true, every
GsmCdmaPhone gets a NoSubscriptionRadioPowerController. It votes the
cellular radio of that phone off with an internal radio-off reason
(RADIO_POWER_REASON_NO_SUBSCRIPTION = 1000) while the phone has no
active subscription, and withdraws the vote as soon as one appears.

A phone has no subscription when SubscriptionManagerService maps no
subscription to its slot and the SIM state is final: ABSENT,
CARD_IO_ERROR, CARD_RESTRICTED, or NOT_READY with an empty eUICC profile
or with uicc applications disabled on the inserted card. A PIN, PUK or
network locked SIM keeps its subscription mapped (the ICCID is readable),
so the radio stays on for the unlock flow and limited service. UNKNOWN,
READY and NOT_READY while applications load are transitional and also
keep the radio on, so the radio is never cut before the SIM state is
known at boot, during a SIM refresh, or while the user re-enables a SIM.

The vote is applied only after the no-subscription state has held for
30 s, and is never applied while the radio is in use for an emergency:
a Telecom emergency call, any call on any phone or IMS phone, emergency
callback mode, emergency SMS mode, EmergencyStateTracker call/ECBM/SCBM
when domain selection is used, or an enabled satellite session. While
blocked it rechecks every 60 s. An emergency call clears all radio-off
reasons through setRadioPower(forEmergencyCall=true); the controller
observes the radio turning on, waits for the emergency session and ECBM
to end, and then applies the vote again. Devices that support OEM
satellite keep the radio on, since SatelliteController refuses to enable
satellite while the cellular radio is off.

Inputs: SubscriptionManagerService onSubscriptionChanged and
onUiccApplicationsEnabledChanged, the carrier config change for this
slot (sent once the SIM state is final), and RIL radio-on. The decision
is per phone, so on multi-SIM devices only the empty or disabled slot
is switched off. The reason is internal to frameworks/opt/telephony;
ServiceStateTracker treats it like any other entry in its reason set and
dumps it as 1000. TelephonyManager#getRadioPowerOffReasons reports it to
privileged callers as an unnamed value; no public API changes.

Test: atest NoSubscriptionRadioPowerControllerTest (not run)
---
diff --git a/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/GsmCdmaPhone.java b/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/GsmCdmaPhone.java
index ef655d7..c2d5251 100644
